>
  <h2>1. How CrockBites Uses Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files stored by your web browser when you visit a website. CrockBites uses strictly necessary first-party cookies to keep signed-in members authenticated and to protect accounts against Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF), along with browser local storage for kitchen convenience features.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Essential First-Party Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    When you register, sign in, or manage the site, CrockBites sets the following essential cookies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>crockbites_user_session</code>: An HTTP-only, cryptographically random session token that keeps you signed in to your member account for up to 30 days (or until you sign out). Only a SHA-256 hash of this token is stored in our Cloudflare D1 database.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>crockbites_user_csrf</code>: A security token paired with your active session to verify that actions such as saving a favorite recipe, submitting or editing a review, or updating your profile originate from you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>crockbites_admin</code> &amp; <code>crockbites_admin_csrf</code>: Isolated authentication and CSRF cookies used exclusively by authorized site administrators when managing recipes or moderating spam.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Browser Local Storage</h2>
  <p>
    Public recipe pages provide interactive tools—including US/Metric measurement conversion, serving-size scaling, Cooking Mode step tracking, and kitchen timers. Your browser may store these non-personal display preferences locally on your device so they are remembered between page loads.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Infrastructure &amp; Security Technologies</h2>
  <p>
    CrockBites is hosted on Cloudflare Pages and Workers, with recipe photography served via Cloudinary. Cloudflare may set security or edge-routing cookies where necessary to detect malicious traffic and protect login and API endpoints.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Advertising &amp; Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>
    To keep our recipes free to read and print, CrockBites may display contextual or personalized advertisements served by Google AdSense or certified advertising partners:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user&rsquo;s prior visits to this website or other websites on the internet.</li>
    <li>Google&rsquo;s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users based on their visit to CrockBites and/or other sites on the internet.</li>
    <li>You may opt out of personalized advertising at any time by visiting <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google My Ad Center</a> or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info/choices</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Managing or Disabling Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can configure your browser to block or delete cookies at any time. Public recipes, ingredient scaling, unit conversion, and print views work without account cookies. However, blocking essential first-party cookies will prevent you from signing in, saving favorite recipes, or submitting community reviews.
  </p>
</TextPage>
